{
  // Deployment config for https://headwater.tools/, which is the target that
  // the https://w3id.org/headwater/ permanent identifier redirects to.
  //
  // There is no Worker script. The project serves static files and nothing
  // else, so there is no "main" entry point.
  //
  // WHAT THE DIRECTORY BELOW IS, AND WHY IT IS NOT `./site`
  //
  //   The site has two halves. `site/` is hand-built and committed byte for
  //   byte, and HW-DR-0037 governs it by name. `.headwater/site-build/` is
  //   what `mkdocs build --strict` renders from the corpus under `docs/` —
  //   the specification, the decisions, the obligations, the tutorial — and
  //   git ignores it, because every byte of it is recomputable.
  //
  //   `tools/site/assemble-site.sh` composes the two into `.headwater/site-deploy`,
  //   the generated half first and the hand-built half last, so a path that
  //   both halves carry is served with the committed bytes. That directory is
  //   what this deploy serves, and HW-DR-0047 rules the arrangement.
  //
  //   So the name below points at a directory that no commit carries. It
  //   exists only because the deploy job ran, which is the one thing this
  //   file depends on and cannot state itself.
  //
  // WHAT RUNS BEFORE THIS FILE IS READ (#1273, HW-DR-0097)
  //
  //   The `Deploy the site` job of `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, on a push to
  //   `main` after every gating job of that push is green. It runs
  //   `tools/site/deploy-site.sh`, which renders the generated half, runs
  //   `tools/site/assemble-site.sh`, fills the figures of the assembled pages
  //   from a run of the engine, adds the APT repository, and then runs
  //   `npx wrangler deploy` from the repository root, which is where it reads
  //   this file. The job needs the repository secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`
  //   and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.
  //
  //   Until #1273 Cloudflare Workers Builds ran `tools/site/cloudflare-build.sh`
  //   and deployed. That integration cannot wait for CI and has no engine to
  //   measure the figures with, so it is to be disconnected in the Worker's
  //   Builds settings. While it stays connected, `cloudflare-build.sh` refuses
  //   each build that would serve a blank figure, and that build publishes
  //   nothing.
  //
  //   If the deploy job stops running, this directory is absent and nothing
  //   deploys. Restore the job first, and only then change the name below.
  "name": "headwater",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-11",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./.headwater/site-deploy"
  }
}
